{"type":"message","id":"b7f2b803","parentId":"6842b353","timestamp":"2026-03-29T07:03:44.910Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants me to generate images for the diagram-related questions in the exam paper. Let me identify which questions need images:\n\n1. Question 2 - Plant cell structure diagram (asking which part contains chloroplast)\n2. Question 21 - A diagram showing two beakers on a balance (osmosis experiment)\n3. Question 26 - Plant cell structure diagram (for labeling)\n4. Question 27 - Heart structure diagram\n5. Question 29 - Urine formation process diagram\n6. Question 30 - Digestive system diagram\n7. Question 31 - Ecosystem diagram (energy flow and material cycling)\n8. Question 33 - Plant transpiration experiment setup\n\nI'll generate these images one by one. Let me start generating them now.","thinkingSignature":"cbb3924c799a67b621ad905cbb5bc32f36005382a96a77ae2f684213d623cb91"},{"type":"text","text":"好的频哥！我来把试卷中需要图片的题目逐一画出来～\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_qidf973v9r2s_1","name":"image_generate","arguments":{"prompt":"Simple biology diagram of plant cell structure for middle school exam, labeled with numbers ① ② ③ ④, showing: ① cell wall, ② cell membrane, ③ cytoplasm, ④ nucleus, ⑤ chloroplast, ⑥ vacuole. Clean black and white line drawing, clear labels, educational style","filename":"plant_cell"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_qidf973v9r2s_2","name":"image_generate","arguments":{"prompt":"Simple middle school biology diagram showing two beakers on a balance scale. Left beaker contains a white radish root piece suspended in liquid, right beaker contains liquid only. The balance is level. Clean black and white line drawing, educational style","filename":"osmosis_beaker"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_qidf973v9r2s_3","name":"image_generate","arguments":{"prompt":"Simple biology diagram of heart structure for middle school exam, showing four chambers labeled 1-4, with arr